{
 "type": "FeatureCollection",
 "about": "Honolua Bay on the afternoon of 1 May 1976, when Hōkūleʻa left for Tahiti (DESIGN.md §14): the canoe at her anchor and under sail, the outrigger canoe that carried the crew out, the escort, the people on the beach and the cliffs, the names of the bay and its point, and the streams. DATA.md “Vessels and crowds, in a district” gives the schema; RESEARCH.md §18 says what each feature rests on. Times are Hawaiʻi standard time and approximate, for the crew had given up their watches; positions in the bay are inferred from the accounts, none of which maps them.",
