    "tellings": [
     {
      "source": "lewis-1977-topics",
      "says": "Next day, 1st May 1976, we unbrailed the sails and put to sea around 1500."
     },
     {
      "source": "lewis-1976-natgeo",
      "says": "Conch-shell trumpets blared from shore as Capt. Kawika Kapahulehua ordered Hokuleʻa’s sails unbrailed and her anchor raised."
     },
     {
      "source": "finney-1979-way-to-tahiti",
      "says": "“Let go! Let go!” shouted Kawika. Only a thin line tied the canoe to the land. … The canoe began to move out. … First we let out the big sail forward, then the smaller sail aft."
     }
    ],
    "note": "She leaves the bay under her own sails: the accounts read give no tow and no paddling, the big sail forward let out first and then the one aft. The line of her course across the bay is not recorded; here down the middle of the bay to its mouth."
   },
