    "sources": [
     "finney-1979-way-to-tahiti",
     "lewis-1976-natgeo",
     "lewis-1977-topics"
    ],
    "tellings": [
     {
      "source": "finney-1979-way-to-tahiti",
      "says": "Kawika guided us out of the bay that had sheltered us since arriving from Honolulu. We skirted the waves curving around the headland. Then the full force of the trades hit us as we broke away from the lee of the cliffs. The canoe surged forward, her sails drawing her into the open ocean as we headed north."
     },
     {
      "source": "lewis-1977-topics",
      "says": "The heavy-laden Hokuleʻa pitched into the seas as she came out from under the land and headed north on the starboard tack. The northeast trades were variable in direction but generally from east-northeast, force 3 (8–12 knots). The weather was mainly cloudy."
     }
    ],
    "note": "Out of the bay and round Līpoa Point, the headland on its north-east side, which Finney does not name; then north on the starboard tack with the trade wind over the bow from the east-north-east. How close she passed the point is not given."
   },
