    "tellings": [
     {
      "source": "lewis-1977-topics",
      "says": "At Piailug’s direction, we came about at midnight when we were roughly 30 miles offshore, and tacked once more at 0900 on May 2nd two miles off Huelo, Maui."
     },
     {
      "source": "lewis-1976-natgeo",
      "says": "“First we go northeast, go around Maui and Big Island. This be maybe three days.”"
     }
    ],
    "note": "The first long tack, north from the bay, as far as the district reaches; she came about that night well out to sea and worked east past Maui and Hawaiʻi Island before turning south. The line is the heading the accounts give, not a fix."
   },
